  "articleBody": "Google AI Overviews are changing how people get answers online, and businesses often wonder if their existing website is prepared for this new landscape. The truth is, while there aren't special 'AI Overviews' buttons to click, foundational web practices are more important than ever. Think of it as making your content so clear and useful that AI can't help but cite it.\n\nFirst, your site needs to be easily crawlable and indexed by search engines. If Google's bots can't properly access and understand your pages, they certainly won't appear in AI Overviews. This means having clean code, a functional `robots.txt`, and a well-structured sitemap. Heavy JavaScript or obscure navigation can often hinder this.\n\nNext, focus on usefulness and accuracy. Google's guidance highlights that pages must meet ordinary Search technical requirements and be eligible for a snippet. This means your content needs to be high-quality, relevant, and directly answer user questions. AI Overviews will pull from pages that are authoritative and helpful, not just keyword-stuffed.\n\nYour pages should be organized around clear customer questions. Instead of broad service pages, consider creating dedicated pages or sections that address specific questions your prospects are asking. This makes it much easier for AI to identify and extract the precise answer it needs to include in an overview or generated response.\n\nMake sure your business information is visible and specific. This includes your services, service areas, qualifications, and contact methods. If this key data is buried in images or interactive elements, AI systems will struggle to find and verify it. Clarity and directness are paramount.\n\nFinally, validate your structured data. If you're using JSON-LD schema, ensure it accurately reflects the visible content on your page. Discrepancies can confuse AI systems and undermine trust. The schema should reinforce, not contradict, what users see and read on your site.\n\n**What to Prepare Before You Start**\n\nBefore diving into AI Overviews optimization, gather your core business information: services offered, primary locations, typical customer questions, and any existing FAQ content. A professional technical audit can help identify crawlability and indexing issues. Also, consider who your target audience is and what specific problems they are trying to solve when they search online.\n\nAI Visibility Solutions helps businesses, especially those in competitive local markets, by creating an 'AI Resource Library' specifically engineered for machine consumption. We ensure your expertise is seen, understood, and cited by Google AI Overviews and other answer engines. If you're ready to move beyond just ranking and truly become the answer, let's connect.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
